rocmlirTriton LLVM source patch
===============================

Upstream base : llvm/llvm-project 62b7cf9623fc310525f39ed69aaecc318a909731
Vendored tree : ROCm/rocmlirTriton 28a5a7a40cfd6aceab0047c7fc92cb5cf90b6540
                (external/llvm-project)

rocmlirTriton vendors LLVM with git subtree and commits its downstream changes
directly onto the imported upstream revision. The records under its
llvm-patches/ directory are provenance for the next upstream bump, not build
inputs, and they cannot be replayed onto clean upstream: patch208280 reverts a
downstream-only fix (#207473) whose own record was dropped, so its pre-image
does not exist in any reachable tree.

This patch is generated from the vendored tree itself, so every file below is
byte-identical to rocmlirTriton's. It carries only sources hip-ep compiles; the
LLVM/MLIR lit-test expectations that the records also update are omitted,
because hip-ep builds LLVM as libraries and never runs check-llvm.

Regenerate after a rocmlirTriton bump:

  # 1. Check out llvm-project at the new upstream base.
  # 2. Overlay the vendored sources for the files this patch touches:
  #      git -C <rocmlirTriton> archive HEAD -- \
  #          $(sed -n 's|^--- a/|external/llvm-project/|p' <this file>) \
  #        | tar -x -C <llvm-project> --strip-components=2
  # 3. Run `git add -N .` so newly added files are included, then write
  #    `git diff` to this file and restore this header.
